  "reason": "The Butler panel now accepts messages while Butler answers. send() is split into prepareButlerRequest (no turn state), a shared runButlerStream (browser actions, pending-action setters, confirmations, saved answer) and send(). While Butler is busy, the composer queues the message in Core's follow-up queue for Butler's chat via useChatQueue (chained, ordered writes; composer clears at once and restores on failure). A ButlerQueue list edits, reorders, removes, pauses, resumes, clears and retries items. The device that queued an item follows its turn with followChatTurn (registered as Butler conversation protocol in the workflow registry) after reading the saved transcript, so its browser actions apply; items this page never saw waiting are only read from the transcript. Device-only commands use a separate deviceBusy flag and run immediately. Stop moves to the activity row. Docs and product help describe the queue; the Playwright area butler-queue covers the real-Core LAN journey. Python: product-help digest and queue/subagent help searches, Playwright impact manifest tests and Butler workflow registry tests. Frontend: new ButlerQueue tests (queue while busy, ordered rapid submits, no duplicated context, following and applying a queued browser action, not following another device's or an old finished item, needs-review retry/resume), the Butler panel suites and subagent tests. Playwright: area:butler-queue on all eight assistant real-Core projects.",
  "exclusions": "Node IDs exclude tests that fail identically on origin/main: tests/test_playwright_impact.py::test_full_manifest_covers_every_product_browser_spec_without_filters (ios-shell-real-core.spec.ts missing from full_include) and tests/v3/test_butler_workflow_registry.py::test_reviewed_workflow_registry_matches_ui_api_calls; tests/v3/test_product_knowledge.py is limited to the digest and Butler help tests because test_product_search_finds_headless_core_and_paired_butler_cli fails on main. No Core Python source changes, so no Core behaviour suites; Core's existing queue already accepts Butler follow-ups (exercised end to end by the real-Core journey). No native changes. Mocked interface.spec.ts journeys are not selected: the real-Core area covers desktop, Chromium and WebKit.",
